From d28899885d30063c8bb568848d5357cbf104520e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Arzt <bill@tlon.io>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:44:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] compile: bounds-check the call frame against the slot table

CompileCallArgsAndReturn places a callee's arguments and results above
every slot currently in use and marks the result slots in m3Slots without
checking the index. A function with a long chain of calls, each consuming
the previous result (about 2,000 on a 4,000-slot table), walks topSlot past
d_m3MaxFunctionSlots and writes beyond the array into the rest of
M3Compilation and the runtime that embeds it. Loading such a module
corrupts the code page lists and crashes the host.

Refuse to compile with m3Err_functionStackOverflow instead, as the other
slot allocators already do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/m3_compile.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/m3_compile.c b/source/m3_compile.c
index 624c86f..fd7c9ea 100644
--- a/source/m3_compile.c
+++ b/source/m3_compile.c
@@ -1542,6 +1542,12 @@ _       (Pop (o));
     u16 numArgs = GetFuncTypeNumParams (i_type);
     u16 numRets = GetFuncTypeNumResults (i_type);
 
+    // the callee's args and results are placed above every slot in use, so
+    // a long chain of calls climbs the slot table. refuse to compile, rather
+    // than write past the end of m3Slots.
+    _throwif (m3Err_functionStackOverflow,
+              (u32) topSlot + ((u32) numArgs + numRets) * c_ioSlotCount > d_m3MaxFunctionSlots);
+
     u16 argTop = topSlot + (numArgs + numRets) * c_ioSlotCount;
 
     while (numArgs--)
-- 
